# ⛔ HARD RULE — Supplify Mobile Parity

**This rule is non-negotiable. Every qualifying change must be reflected in BOTH mobile repos and in the documentation before the task is done.**

## Mobile repos (BOTH must be updated)

- `C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile` — React Native / Expo (Android)
- `C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile-ios` — React Native / Expo (iOS)

There is also an in-repo Expo workspace at `mobile-work/` — update it too when it contains relevant code.

---

## What ALWAYS requires updating both mobile repos

| Change in this repo | Required mobile action |
|---|---|
| New or modified API endpoint | Update API client, request/response types in both mobile repos |
| Auth flow change (OIDC, token, session, OTP, driver bypass) | Update auth hooks, token storage, session guards |
| New or changed RBAC permission key | Update permission checks and navigation guards |
| New or changed feature flag key | Update feature gates and upgrade prompts |
| Order or fulfillment lifecycle change | Update restaurant / supplier / driver flows |
| GPS / ETA / delivery tracking change | Update tracking hooks; keep `deliveryEtaDisplay` helpers in sync |
| Notification event or push payload change | Update notification handlers and deep-link routing |
| New required env var | Add to `mobile-work/.env.example`, `C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile/.env.example`, `C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile-ios/.env.example` |
| Type change in `apps/web/src/types/index.ts` | Port the change to mobile type definitions |

---

## When mobile can be skipped (explicit documentation required)

These change types do NOT require mobile updates:

- Admin-only platform features (no mobile admin surface)
- Web-only layout, animation, or CSS changes
- Server-side cron, migration, or infra changes with no client contract change

**Even when skipping: you MUST add a dated entry to `docs/mobile/MOBILE_FEATURE_PARITY.md` stating what changed and why mobile is not affected.**

---

## ⛔ MANDATORY — Docs must be updated

After any qualifying change, update:

1. **`docs/mobile/MOBILE_FEATURE_PARITY.md`** — dated entry always (implemented or skipped-with-reason)
2. **Domain docs** (`docs/features/`, `docs/architecture/`, `docs/operations/`) — update if the change affects documented behavior
3. **`docs/guides/environment-variables.md`** — add any new env vars
4. **`docs/admin/feature-flags.md`** — add any new feature keys
5. **`docs/architecture/rbac-overview.md`** — add any new permission keys or roles

---

## Completion checklist (must satisfy before "done")

- [ ] `C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile` updated **or** skip reason documented
- [ ] `C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile-ios` updated **or** skip reason documented
- [ ] `mobile-work/` updated if it contains relevant code
- [ ] Types in sync with `apps/web/src/types/index.ts`
- [ ] Mobile typecheck passes: `cd C:/myProjects/supplify-mobile && npx tsc --noEmit`
- [ ] `docs/mobile/MOBILE_FEATURE_PARITY.md` has a dated entry for this change
- [ ] All affected domain docs updated

